# NestJS

- `script` files are TypeScript. Use `@Module`, `@Controller`, `@Injectable` as in `src/app.module.ts`.
- Inject `ConfigService` for env values. Do not read `process.env` in controllers or services except in `src/config/env.ts` and bootstrap.
- Keep HTTP handlers thin: controller → service.
- Add features as Nest modules under `src/`, not as a second framework.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
import { AppService } from './app.service';

// ✅ GOOD
import { AppService } from './app.service.js';
```
